From: Amperstrand <141745238+Amperstrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:44:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Suppress warnings from generated RAL code

The register access layer is generated (ral-registers) and emits three
warning classes in every downstream build:

- unexpected_cfgs for the `nosync` and `rtfm` cfg switches the
  generator emits,
- unused_imports and dead_code in the per-peripheral modules.

Add crate-level allows so downstream `-D warnings` builds stay clean.

Independent of the F469 fix; if targeted #[allow]s (or generator-side
fixes) are preferred, this patch can be dropped from the series.
---
 src/lib.rs | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
index e2b9a06..6b44ce0 100644
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -1,6 +1,11 @@
 //! USB peripheral driver for Synopsys USB OTG peripherals.
 
 #![no_std]
+// Suppress warnings for cfg features (nosync, rtfm) used in generated RAL code
+#![allow(unexpected_cfgs)]
+// Suppress warnings for unused imports and dead code in generated RAL code
+#![allow(unused_imports)]
+#![allow(dead_code)]
 
 #[cfg(all(feature = "fs", feature = "hs"))]
 compile_error!("choose only one USB mode");
